======================================================================
(1) Symbolic re-derivation of the crossing condition from scratch
======================================================================
ratio(j) = t_{j+1}/t_j = -(g - 1)*(j + m + 1)*(j + m - n)/((j + 1)*(j - n))
difference vs ATTEMPT.md's stated crossing-condition LHS: 0
CONFIRMED: the crossing-condition expression in ATTEMPT.md Sec.4 is
exactly the term ratio t_{j+1}/t_j -- an accurate restatement, not
an unjustified assertion.

======================================================================
(2) Cross-validate j* via brute-force ARGMAX (different method) vs
    the ratio-walk method, at a range of (n,m,gamma) NOT identical
    to target's script 03/05 grids
======================================================================
48 checks, 0 mismatches between ratio-walk and brute-force argmax
CONFIRMED: the ratio-walk locator used by the target is not just
self-consistent -- it agrees with an entirely different (brute-force
argmax) computation of the same j*, everywhere tested.

======================================================================
(3) Independent asymptotic derivation via sympy: solve the crossing
    condition for the leading behavior of j as m,n->oo with n->oo
    fastest (m=o(n)), then m,j->oo together.
======================================================================
Taking n->oo at fixed j,m (isolates the (n-j-m)/(n-j)->1 factor):
  limit = (1 - g)*(j + m + 1)/(j + 1)
  matches (j+m+1)/(j+1)*(1-g) exactly, confirming the n->oo step of
  ATTEMPT.md's derivation.

Step 2: setting this equal to 1 and solving for j in terms of m:
  exact solution j = [-m - 1 + m/g]
  simplified: -m - 1 + m/g

Step 3: leading behavior as m -> infinity of this exact j(m):
  lim_{m->oo} j(m)/m = (1 - g)/g
  ATTEMPT.md's claimed limit (1-g)/g: (1 - g)/g  difference: 0
CONFIRMED INDEPENDENTLY (fully symbolic, sympy limit -- not just the
informal 'drop O(1) shifts' argument in the prose): j*/m -> (1-g)/g
as m->infinity (after first sending n->infinity / m=o(n)), i.e.
j* ~ m(1-gamma)/gamma is a mathematically correct leading-order
asymptotic of the EXACT discrete crossing condition.

